From 737d543442c08c54d6c016474a350f8e39e8a5ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: obotkov <obotkov@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:33:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] vpn-admin: UpCloud hosting with server creation via
 cloud-init
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- UpCloud accounts with an API token (Bearer ucat_…) and an optional public
  SSH key for new servers; balance in the account currency.
- Servers with IPs from /ip_address; zones with flags; plans with prices from
  /price (cents per hour, month capped at 672 hours), GPU plans hidden.
- Cloud-init templates require a login key: the admin passes a throwaway key
  whose private half is discarded and the setup script deletes it.
- Delete stops the server and removes it with its disks.
- Credential fields can be optional.
